# Smart Route Optimization & 'Whole Road' Analysis

This plan outlines the implementation of a comprehensive "Whole Road" analysis and a smart route optimizer that actively avoids high-pothole areas by requesting new paths from the mapping service.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **API Performance**: Requesting a route with many `avoid_polygons` can slow down the response time significantly. I will implement a clustering algorithm to group nearby potholes into single "exclusion zones" to keep the request efficient.
> **Scan Radius**: For the "Whole Road" calculation, I will increase the search radius from 25m to 70m. This ensures that potholes on the same street (but different lanes) or at intersections are captured in the score.

## Proposed Changes

### Map Screen Component

#### [MODIFY] [map_screen.dart](file:///c:/ssdd/flutter/lib/map_screen.dart)

- **'Whole Road' Score Calculation**:
    - Update `_processRoutes` to use an expanded search radius (70m).
    - Implement a "Road Health" indicator for each route (e.g., "Smooth", "Caution", "Poor").
    - Calculate "Potholes per KM" to give a more relative score.

- **Smart Optimization (Avoidance)**:
    - **Clustering Logic**: Create a helper method `_getAvoidPolygons()` that:
        1. Identifies potholes within the general "BBox" of the trip.
        2. Groups potholes within 50-100m of each other.
        3. Generates GeoJSON Polygons for these high-risk areas.
    - **ORS Request Update**: Modify `_calculateRoute` to accept an optional `avoidPolygons` parameter.
        - If present, include it in the `options.avoid_polygons` field of the ORS POST request.

- **UI Updates**:
    - **Optimization Button**: Add a "Smart Optimize" button (e.g., a magic wand or refresh icon) that appears when a destination is selected.
    - **Enhanced Route Cards**: Display the calculated "Health" status of each route.
    - **Avoidance Visualization**: Briefly show the "Avoid Areas" (semi-transparent red boxes) on the map during optimization so the user understands what is being avoided.

